  "supplementary_definitions": {
    "path": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/00b1/lemmadeck/.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-181/tmp/d1289-n101-t11-first-choice/supplementary-definitions.json",
    "file_sha256": "a3fe0c6a7814303561fe6e8665962f79d7de8d6dca47a5f179113ccdc4a21763",
    "canonical_sha256": "029e838a68c1f02c34dcfea7a59cc09909619a97310b363f6a15cd70d1f6326e",
    "policy": "Explicit selected exact text UTF-8 SHA-256 values retained outside seeds and linked from FIRST source solutions",
    "authorities": [
      {
        "path": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/00b1/lemmadeck/ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/10p/editions/modern-us-neutral/lessons/phy10-c2-s4-n101/lesson.json",
        "file_sha256": "9fefdc554e4ec5d6b983cda02fad764f2d88ea86e509a7eb079bd4878a8e5f31",
        "canonical_sha256": "2ee33aadb0e65d474b693b8ffea982791e279b42cc2bbed7d64488740662698a",
        "role": "Definitions only; not answer authority",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "block": 1,
            "text": "原书从能量守恒定律和随速度变化的“质量”来说明质能联系。\n这里沿用原书的历史“相对论质量”概念，不把它与物体的不变静质量混为一谈。\n给容器中的气体加热，就是使气体获得能量。\n\n分子的无规则热运动速度与温度有关，加热时会增大。\n根据公式(8.9)，速度增大意味着各分子的历史相对论质量增大，而不是各分子的不变静质量因运动而增大。\n\n这里在气体整体静止的参考系中，比较容器中同一份气体，且没有物质流失。\n气体保留所获得的热能时，内能增加，整体的不变质量也增加，说明气体的质量与能量之间存在联系。",
            "text_utf8_sha256": "5d8ba31351f0d77e7cecd77b02c8ce48a12478abcf80ab2d7188f01e132b2523"
          },
          {
            "block": 7,
            "text": "**爱因斯坦公式**。\n爱因斯坦利用相对论得到能量与质量之间简洁而普遍的关系。\n这里的能量是所选参考系中的总能量，质量沿用原书的历史相对论质量定义，公式为：\n$E=mc^2=\\frac{m_0c^2}{\\sqrt{1-\\frac{v^2}{c^2}}}$ (8.12)",
            "text_utf8_sha256": "df9dc68a6efcc761abb6d583c8e8ea93c910969595844dad1d939e80461895f3"
          },
          {
            "block": 9,
            "text": "按原书的质量定义，在同一参考系中比较同一系统，系统的总能量改变时，相应的历史相对论质量也改变。\n若系统前后均静止在这个参考系中，比较的就是系统的静能变化，相应质量变化是不变质量的变化：\n$\\Delta m=\\frac{\\Delta E}{c^2}$ (8.13)",
            "text_utf8_sha256": "a2d697de7afc60905322c868b76a70daee68303b8a84fa52b64c5d8ba6618d1a"
          },
          {
            "block": 10,
            "text": "系数$\\frac{1}{c^2}$非常小，因此，要出现明显的质量变化，能量变化必须非常大。\n原书讨论通常条件下的化学反应和加热，认为能量变化小到无法在实验中发现相应的质量变化。\n原书举例说，滚烫的茶壶比冷茶壶的质量大些，但即使用最灵敏的天平，也测不出这个差别。\n\n比较的是同一茶壶及其内容物，在物质不流失且热能保留时的静止状态。\n这里保留的是原书对当时实验能力的说明，不把它当作任何时代都无法测量的断言。\n原书将这种情形与原子核和基本粒子的变化作对比：在后者中，能量变化足够大，相应的质量变化便能被觉察。",
            "text_utf8_sha256": "c149a442823dfbafdd68490439aa253bd575df8946a6f1740f8e71e3a2170e41"
          },
          {
            "block": 14,
            "text": "在这里保留的二阶近似精度内，第二项是通常的低速动能，第一项则是这个结果最有新意的部分。\n第一项给出物体速度为0时的能量，即**静能**$E_0$：\n$E_0=m_0c^2$ (8.15)",
            "text_utf8_sha256": "09bdb374d8dd096a1d6404d90d3679a096e2e8e9f1a39a39b5bf099029b3d6b2"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/00b1/lemmadeck/ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/10p/editions/modern-us-neutral/lessons/phy10-c2-s4-n95/lesson.json",
        "file_sha256": "a5863d400da8b6f6b770d51d140533b19ab97ff581df5a7ddff0ebec71e48707",
        "canonical_sha256": "9753169708c2f498146b9c0cbd32bf0326e3205e1d6895f8b2eef90e253976c4",
        "role": "Definitions only; not answer authority",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "block": 2,
            "text": "在选定的同一惯性参考系中，例如两次闪电击中不同地点，若事件发生时当地同步钟的读数相同，这两个事件就是同时的。\n比较的是事件发生时的钟读数，不是两道闪光到达某个人眼睛的时刻。",
            "text_utf8_sha256": "298e8e6d17e080e061929bf976113a790c4ed04a87415f9aa14e6170a4b20ae0"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/00b1/lemmadeck/.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-181/tmp/d1218-n97-rigid-rod-affected-repair/zh/lesson.template.json",
        "file_sha256": "15004a3cd21dcb279a7d0ccf3ff4b0bc9a7616f300b05a51e3d1ff475c774364",
        "canonical_sha256": "fda0e9a21b368a76962c0a833def1728c68b2bfe0de85e8a01a520c94c5a4da8",
        "role": "Definitions only; not answer authority",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "block": 19,
            "text": "对同一根棒作比较，静长是它最大的纵向测量长度。\n如果改为让棒在参考系 $K$ 中静止，则它在这里的长度为 $l_0$，而在参考系 $K_1$ 中测得的纵向长度按公式(8.2)缩短。\n这符合相对性原理，并不意味着存在优先的惯性参考系。",
            "text_utf8_sha256": "d595d2832704ccbb41f5e1e7dee0c57c2647570de7be5d8649e1e37cc6179010"
          },
          {
            "block": 21,
            "text": "原书引用爱丁格顿，提醒读者这种相互收缩会挑战日常直觉。\n可以比较两根静长相同、分别在两个惯性参考系中静止并沿相对运动方向放置的棒。\n每个参考系中的观察者都测得另一根运动棒比本地静止棒短。\n\n这里比较的是按各自参考系的钟同时记录的两端位置，而不是看到的外观。\n两个参考系对同时性的判定不同，因此这些对称的测量结论并不矛盾。",
            "text_utf8_sha256": "228ca765740f6127e5c6e95257dfdfc92fd43312633ea3334c3747bb5183200c"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/00b1/lemmadeck/.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-181/tmp/d1218-n97-rigid-rod-affected-repair/en/lesson.template.json",
        "file_sha256": "4033bc45572426d1c21925779c768811d1239dac7e3948a11efeca9ce961eb09",
        "canonical_sha256": "585678fdbff0eb62881b077b50c06ed6a47ae38e4f1d2a0fed2494e6f8adff84",
        "role": "Definitions only; not answer authority",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "block": 19,
            "text": "For the same rod, the proper length is its greatest measured longitudinal length.\nIf instead the rod is at rest in frame $K$, its length there is $l_0$, while its longitudinal length measured in frame $K_1$ is contracted according to equation (8.2).\nThis agrees with the relativity principle and does not select a preferred inertial frame.",
            "text_utf8_sha256": "fee8e5aa14a3d5c78d247354ed7b6e3ca3f297e43eed847fa8d2152999b46880"
          },
          {
            "block": 21,
            "text": "The source cites Eddington to note that reciprocal contraction challenges everyday intuition.\nCompare two rods of equal proper length, each at rest in a different inertial frame and aligned with their relative motion.\n\nObservers in each frame measure the other, moving rod to be shorter than their local, stationary rod.\nThey compare endpoint positions recorded simultaneously according to their own frame's clocks, not visual appearances.\nThe frames use different simultaneity conditions, so these symmetric measurements do not contradict each other.",
            "text_utf8_sha256": "26b567e24db807b6048cc6a6bffe5be2392a81eb06ab8f9fb85035b863ce0414"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
